Optimal prime-packing: Q_div (packing capacity) vs q* (first witness) vs tiling correction.
========================================================================================
             M  log10 M  #blocked primes  max blocked prime    q* tiling corr (q*-firstfree)
       1000000 (no valid covering packer)
    1000000000 (no valid covering packer)
 1000000000000 (no valid covering packer)
1000000000000000 (no valid covering packer)
1000000000000000000 (no valid covering packer)

=> q* tracks the prime-packing capacity (# distinct primes 13 speeds<=M can hold = O(log M/loglog));
   tiling correction (free primes that are no-witness) BOUNDED => the crux is ELEMENTARY prime-packing
   + a bounded circle-method correction. q* = O(log M loglog M), constant from the packing.
